{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyMYwc4V7PCy/ieeZOHFloOK"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Simulación del Circuito RLC en el dominio del tiempo\n","Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo\n","\n","## Modelo matemático del sistema\n","\n","Consideramos un circuito RLC compuesto por una resistencia $R$, una inductancia $L$ y un capacitor $C$.\n","La entrada del sistema es el voltaje aplicado $V_i(t)$ y la salida es el voltaje en el capacitor $V_c(t)$.\n","\n","Aplicando la Ley de Kirchhoff de voltajes, la ecuación que describe la dinámica del sistema es:\n","\n","$$ LC \\ddot{V}_c(t) + RC \\dot{V}_c(t) + V_c(t) = V_i(t) $$\n","\n","donde:\n","\n","$R:$ es la resistencia del circuito $[Ω]$,\n","\n","$L:$ es la inductancia $[H]$,\n","\n","$C:$ es la capacitancia $[F]$,\n","\n","$V_i(t):$ es el voltaje de entrada $[V]$,\n","\n","$V_c(t):$ es el voltaje en el capacitor $[V]$.\n","\n","Este modelo corresponde a un sistema lineal de segundo orden."],"metadata":{"id":"b1YzKwe3xOxv"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from scipy.integrate import solve_ivp"],"metadata":{"id":"yctBlzcmxQ0V","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1770221137917,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo","userId":"11821565480340800524"}}},"execution_count":33,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Parámetros del circuito\n","\n","Los valores de los componentes del circuito son: $ R=10Ω$, $L=0.5F$ y $C=0.01F$"],"metadata":{"id":"ad1jx2OB1yzC"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# -----------------------------\n","# Parámetros del sistema\n","# -----------------------------\n","\n","R = 10.0     # Ohm\n","L = 0.5      # Henry\n","C = 0.01     # Farad\n","\n","def Vi(t):\n","    return 1.0  # Voltaje constante (1 V)"],"metadata":{"id":"_NJTX0P3xfYn","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1770221137930,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":11,"user":{"displayName":"Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo","userId":"11821565480340800524"}}},"execution_count":34,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Conversión a un sistema de primer orden\n","\n","Para resolver la ecuación diferencial mediante métodos numéricos, se define el vector de estado:\n","\n","$ x_1(t) = V_c(t) $\n","\n","$ x_2(t) = \\dot{V}_c(t) $\n","\n","Con estas definiciones, el sistema equivalente de primer orden queda dado por:\n","\n","$ \\dot{x}_1(t) = x_2(t) $\n","\n","$ \\dot{x}_2(t) = \\frac{1}{LC} \\left[ V_i(t) - RCx_2(t) - x_1(t) \\right] $"],"metadata":{"id":"FygmY_vgzYxD"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# -----------------------------\n","# Sistema de ecuaciones\n","# -----------------------------\n","\n","def rlc_system(t, x):\n","    x1, x2 = x  # x1 = Vc, x2 = dVc/dt\n","    dx1dt = x2\n","    dx2dt = (1/(L*C)) * (Vi(t) - R*C*x2 - x1)\n","\n","    return [dx1dt, dx2dt]"],"metadata":{"id":"_gn1v5p8xq8o","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1770221137933,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":1,"user":{"displayName":"Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo","userId":"11821565480340800524"}}},"execution_count":35,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Condiciones iniciales\n","\n","Para la simulación se asume que el capacitor se encuentra inicialmente descargado, por lo que:\n","\n","$ V_c(0) = 0 $\n","\n","$ \\dot{V}_c(0) = 0 $"],"metadata":{"id":"pvuhLui90gOG"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# ----------------------------------------------------------\n","# Condiciones iniciales (Asumimos el capacitor descargado)\n","# ----------------------------------------------------------\n","\n","x0 = [0.0, 0.0]  # Vc(0) = 0, dVc/dt(0) = 0"],"metadata":{"id":"3vEBy9OIyGUj","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1770221137935,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":1,"user":{"displayName":"Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo","userId":"11821565480340800524"}}},"execution_count":36,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Intervalo temporal de simulación\n","\n","La simulación se realiza en el intervalo: $ 𝑡 \\in [0,10] $ s"],"metadata":{"id":"vEg8RFxB1R5k"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# -----------------------------\n","# Intervalo de tiempo\n","# -----------------------------\n","\n","t_span = (0, 5)  # segundos\n","t_eval = np.linspace(t_span[0], t_span[1], 1000)"],"metadata":{"id":"-1QL2aZK1jw9","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1770221137978,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":2,"user":{"displayName":"Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo","userId":"11821565480340800524"}}},"execution_count":37,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Resolución numérica del sistema"],"metadata":{"id":"HvacoLEe1EQT"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# -----------------------------\n","# Resolución numérica\n","# -----------------------------\n","\n","solution = solve_ivp(\n","    rlc_system,\n","    t_span,\n","    x0,\n","    t_eval=t_eval\n",")"],"metadata":{"id":"kEU8wYIj1E6g","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1770221137980,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":1,"user":{"displayName":"Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo","userId":"11821565480340800524"}}},"execution_count":38,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Identificación de entrada y salida\n","\n","La entrada del sistema se define como:\n","\n","$ x(t) = V_i(t) $\n","\n","La salida del sistema corresponde al voltaje en el capacitor:\n","\n","$ y(t) = V_c(t) $"],"metadata":{"id":"IrNR9Ww70WsJ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["t = solution.t\n","Vc = solution.y[0]"],"metadata":{"id":"SDpK4Iom0cFg","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1770221137988,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":7,"user":{"displayName":"Maria Isabel Garcia Quimbayo","userId":"11821565480340800524"}}},"execution_count":39,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Resultados\n","\n","Se grafica la evolución temporal del voltaje en el capacitor."],"metadata":{"id":"V4IcQk7B0woj"}},{"cell_type":"code"